## Project purpose
Track a Panini FIFA World Cup 2026 sticker collection. User drops photos of album pages and loose sticker piles into `images/inbox/`. The Cursor agent analyzes each photo with its built-in vision, then calls Python scripts to update the SQLite inventory. No external API keys required.

## Sticker code format
- Team stickers: `{TEAM_CODE}{NUMBER}` — no space, uppercase (e.g. `ARG17`, `SUI6`)
- FWC stickers: `FWC1` through `FWC19`
- Panini logo: `PANINI`
- Always normalize: `.upper().replace(" ", "")`

## Album structure (980 stickers total)
- `PANINI` — Panini logo foil (1)
- `FWC1–FWC8` — Intro foils
- `FWC9–FWC19` — FIFA Museum foils
- 48 teams × 20 stickers: `{TC}1` = badge foil, `{TC}2–12` = players, `{TC}13` = team photo, `{TC}14–20` = players

## Inventory status rules
- `missing` — not yet collected (default for all on first init)
- `owned` — placed in album (set by album page scans)
- `extra` — duplicate/spare for trading (set by extras scans)
- **`owned` is never downgraded** — never overwrite owned → missing

